# The Entropy Workshop's downloadable artifact and its checksum.
#
# -text means git stores and checks out these bytes exactly, with no
# end-of-line translation in either direction. That is not a preference here,
# it is a correctness requirement: the SHA-256 published beside the artifact
# describes specific bytes, and letting git rewrite them on commit or checkout
# made the published checksum describe a file nobody could obtain. Someone
# following the verify instructions got a mismatch and was right to stop.
docs/entropy-offline.html       -text
docs/entropy-offline.html.sha256 -text
*.sh text eol=lf
